    "result_text": "I added `create_access_token(data, token_expire_minutes=None)` to `lnbits/helpers.py`. I haven't run the tests or the app.\n\n- **Behavior:** it drops `None` values from `data` and adds an `exp` claim. The expiry is `token_expire_minutes` if you pass it, otherwise `settings.auth_token_expire_minutes`. It signs with HS256 using `settings.auth_secret_key`.\n- **Origin:** I took it from the catalog pattern `auth.lnbits_access_token@v1` and kept its `# pcat:` marker above the function.\n- **Existing callers:** `lnbits/core/views/auth_api.py` and several tests already imported `create_access_token` from `lnbits.helpers`. It wasn't defined there, so this also fills that gap. Those callers pass `data=` and `token_expire_minutes=`, which matches the signature.\n- **Catalog check:** the first `check_code` run flagged a high-severity \"library swapped\" deviation. That came from checking the function without the file's imports. With `jwt`, `datetime` and `settings` included, there are no deviations and no approvals are needed."
